WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.000
Learn how to add an SSH public key to SUSE Virtualization. Virtual machines that use the key let you log in without a password.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.950
In the navigation menu, expand Advanced,

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:16.180
and select SSH Keys.

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:18.660
Select Create.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:24.590
Choose the namespace. Virtual machines in this namespace can use the key.

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:26.710
Give the key a name.

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:32.060
Paste the public key. You can also load it from a file with Read from File.

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:34.500
Select Create.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:39.660
SUSE Virtualization validates the key and shows its fingerprint.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:43.110
To use the key, go to Virtual Machines

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:45.780
and select Create.

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:48.820
In the same namespace,

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:54.390
open the SSH key list on the Basics tab and pick the key.

00:00:54.390 --> 00:01:02.580
When the virtual machine starts, cloud-init adds this key to the default user's authorized keys.

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:08.761
Your SSH key is stored and ready to use. Next, you create a Linux virtual machine.
